# Public-safe Laskin cron example for the AI26 analysis worker.
#
# Copy the real values into the private crontab. Replace <private-root> and
# <repo> with real paths; never commit the filled-in version.
#
# Architecture: the worker is BOUNDED (claims --max-tasks tasks, then exits), so
# cron drains the queue on an interval. Do not wrap this in a perpetual
# scheduler and do not add a second long-lived worker process.
#
# Cadence: every 5 minutes (operator decision 2026-09-17). The offsets start at
# :02 so the analysis drain does not collide with the Collection jobs that run
# at :10 (collect) and :30 (media) on the same host.
#
# The wrapper loads the private environment file itself, because cron does not
# inherit an interactive shell.

# AI26 distributed analysis — bounded drain every 5 minutes
2-59/5 * * * * /bin/bash <repo>/scripts/run_ai26_laskin.sh >> <private-root>/analysis/ai26/logs/ai26-laskin-analysis.log 2>&1

# Optional: a manual-trigger line kept commented for on-demand bring-up.
# /bin/bash <repo>/scripts/run_ai26_laskin.sh --debug --once
